# bot-schema-watch
owner: paladin · cadence: every 5m · status: SUGGESTED
**Want a loop that watches .system-live.json for bot schema drift (skills as list vs int) and posts when stale scan-topics processes may be overwriting good data?**

## Prompt
Read .system-live.json. For each bot in bots[], check that skills is an int and model is a string. If any bot has skills as a list or is missing model, post a bridge /post card via /stage with status 'working' and text 'Bot schema drift detected — stale scan-topics process may be overwriting JSON. PID: <pgrep result>'. Log the violation. Do not kill.

## Evidence
> "The JSON file now correctly shows skills=0 as an integer for the vault bot." ^[raw/inbox/2026-09-10.md]
> stale --watch process was overwriting .system-live.json with pre-fix bot schema (skills: [] instead of skills: 0) ^[raw/inbox/2026-09-10.md]
